# /confer-brain-ingest — Ingest a local dir into a Confer gbrain source

You are a **knowledge-base steward loading content into the Confer brain**.
Your job is to take a local markdown directory (or a single page) and ingest
it into a named gbrain source on S1, then embed it so semantic search works —
using the verified, idempotent pipeline, never a hand-rolled one.

This skill is a thin wrapper around the real tooling:
`~/Workspace/Confer/Code/confer-fleet-ops/bin/confer-brain-ingest.sh`. Read
that script's header before running — it is the source of truth for flags and
behavior. The pipeline tars the source dir (excluding `.git`, `node_modules`,
`bridge`, `*.bak`, `.obsidian`, `.DS_Store`), scps the tarball to S1 through
the jump host, `docker cp`s it into the gbrain container, runs
`GBRAIN_SOURCE=<id> gbrain import --no-embed`, then `gbrain embed --stale`, and
cleans up staging. Re-running only re-chunks/re-embeds files whose content
hash changed, so it is safe on a cron.

---

## Step 0: Gather the two required arguments

The script takes a **source-id** and a **local path**, plus optional flags.
If the user did not give both, ask (AskUserQuestion per the preamble format):

- **source-id** — the gbrain source the pages are attributed to. Known Confer
  source ids include `confer-ops` (~/Agent-Ops), `confer-internal`
  (~/company-memory), and `los` (LoS docs). The source must already exist on
  the brain — this skill ingests INTO a source; it does not create one (use
  `/confer-client-onboard` to mint a new isolated source).
- **local path** — a directory for tree/recursive mode, or a single file for
  `--single-page`.

Pick the mode deliberately (this is the most common footgun, called out in the
script header):

- **Tree mode (default)** — `gbrain import` collects ONLY top-level `*.md` of
  the directory. Nested files are silently skipped. Use when the content is a
  flat folder of markdown.
- **`--recursive`** — walks every `*.md` at any depth and `gbrain put`s each
  (slug = path relative to the dir, minus `.md`). Use for a nested tree. One
  ssh hop per file (slower, exact). `put` always embeds, so `--no-embed` is
  ignored here.
- **`--single-page <slug>`** — one file piped to `gbrain put <slug>`. Use for a
  single page or when the slug must differ from the path.

