## Step 1: Dry-run first (always)

Never ingest blind. Run `--dry-run` to print every step (tar/scp/docker
exec) without writing anything, and show the resolved container + mode banner:

```bash
~/Workspace/Confer/Code/confer-fleet-ops/bin/confer-brain-ingest.sh \
  <source-id> <local-path> --dry-run
```

Read back the banner to the user: the `source-id`, resolved `source` path, the
`mode` line (tree / recursive / single-page), and the `embed` line. Confirm
this matches their intent before the real run. If the banner shows tree mode
but the user expected nested files ingested, switch to `--recursive`.

---

## Step 2: Real ingest

Run the same command without `--dry-run`. Pass through the user's flags
verbatim — do not paraphrase paths or slugs:

```bash
# Tree mode (top-level *.md), import + embed --stale:
~/Workspace/Confer/Code/confer-fleet-ops/bin/confer-brain-ingest.sh \
  <source-id> <local-dir>

# Nested tree (every *.md at any depth):
~/Workspace/Confer/Code/confer-fleet-ops/bin/confer-brain-ingest.sh \
  <source-id> <local-dir> --recursive

# Single page with an explicit slug:
~/Workspace/Confer/Code/confer-fleet-ops/bin/confer-brain-ingest.sh \
  <source-id> <local-file> --single-page <slug>

# Keyword-only now, embed later (tree mode only; --single-page/--recursive
# always embed):
~/Workspace/Confer/Code/confer-fleet-ops/bin/confer-brain-ingest.sh \
  <source-id> <local-dir> --no-embed
```

The script is `set -euo pipefail` and rolls its own staging cleanup; let it run
to completion. It prints numbered stage markers (`[1/6]`…`[6/6]` in tree mode).
If it exits non-zero, surface its stderr verbatim and STOP — do not retry with
different flags blindly.

### S1 reachability

S1 (`144.126.158.171`) is **reachable only via the jump host**
